// qmomCoagulation: spatially-uniform two-node QMOM with constant-kernel
// Smoluchowski coagulation. Moments are chosen to be a valid positive measure
// (M0 M2 > M1^2, M1 M3 > M2^2) and the explicit horizon stays in that cone.
// The checker reconstructs the closed-form moment trajectory
//   M0(t) = M00/(1+beta M00 t/2), M1 const,
//   M2(t) = M20 + beta M10^2 t,
//   M3(t) = M30 + 3 beta M10 M20 t + (3/2) beta^2 M10^2 t^2
// and independently verifies the two-node Gaussian quadrature reproduces all
// four moments at every reported step.
qmom
{
    beta 0.05;
    m0 1.0;
    m1 1.0;
    m2 1.2;
    m3 1.5;
    dt 0.5;
    steps 20;
    reportEvery 2;
}
